.What this home covers
[%collapsible]
======
This home is a starter kit. It sets up the security work that is done once for its scope, at a basic and proportionate level. "Basic" means that the minimum measures and their evidence are in place. It does not mean ready for certification, and it is not legal advice.

[cols="2,5,5"]
|===
| Framework | In this home | Elsewhere

| NIS2
| Governance (Article 20), the risk-management measures (Article 21(2)), and reporting (Article 23), at a basic level. Each measure has at least one control in the libraries
| The details of the national law, for example registration and sector rules. Check the national law.

| EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA)
| The duties of the organisation: the channel for vulnerability reports, the notifications, and the authority contacts
| The duties for each product, for example risk assessment, SBOM, technical documentation, and conformity assessment. Do them in the development projects of the secure development and EU CRA modules.

| ISO/IEC 27001
| A foundation: scope, policy, roles, assets, risks, targets, and reviews. The roles do not meet all requirements of the standard yet, for example the competence records and a formal analysis of the segregation of duties
| Certification: Statement of Applicability, internal audit, full management review, corrective actions, and the full Annex A. These are in the ISO/IEC 27001 extension.

| EU AI Act
| The obligations of an organisation that uses AI: AI literacy (Article 4), the prohibited practices (Article 5), transparency (Article 50), and the deployers of high-risk AI systems (Article 26), at a basic level, with the AI use basics library
| The obligations of the providers of AI systems, and AI in the products. The AI management system of ISO/IEC 42001.
|===

*What each library covers*

{{#report}}
  "name": "ismsa/reports/homeLibraryCoverage"
{{/report}}

*When you need more*

* To get certified to ISO/IEC 27001, add the ISO/IEC 27001 extension.
* To develop products under the CRA, create development projects with the secure development module, and add the EU CRA module.
* To meet the national law, read the law and the guidance of the authority. For example, in Finland, read the Cybersecurity Act (Kyberturvallisuuslaki) and the recommendations of Traficom.
======
